---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="How a Bluey car at Subiefest started Ghost Subie Adventures — Roman, his wife Michelle, their son Jonah, and Boo the blue heeler, overlanding Texas and beyond."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Preparedness Without Panic</span>
      <h1>How a Bluey car started all of this.</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="split about-split">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          At our first Subiefest, my then-7-year-old son Jonah spotted a Bluey-themed Subaru
          across the lot &mdash; and fell in love. Not just with the car, but with the whole
          idea of it. The club. The people. The wave.
        </p>
        <p>
          We joined Natalie&rsquo;s San Antonio car club that year, and she made Jonah feel like
          he belonged from day one. We&rsquo;ve been Subaru people ever since.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Ghost is our white Subaru Forester &mdash; and it&rsquo;s the family daily driver
          first. School runs, grocery runs, San Antonio traffic. But most weekends, it earns
          its name: loaded with camp gear, pointed at the horizon, gone.
        </p>
        <p>
          I&rsquo;m Roman. I&rsquo;m a U.S. Army veteran &mdash; deployed around the world and
          supported special operations &mdash; and these days my mission is simpler: my wife
          Michelle, our son Jonah, our blue heeler Boo, and I camp, explore, and overland
          across Texas and beyond &mdash; and I document all of it here and on the Ghost Subie
          Adventures Podcast.
        </p>
        <p>
          The philosophy is simple: <strong>Preparedness Without Panic.</strong> Real family
          camping. Real skills. Real gear that&rsquo;s actually been slept in, cooked on, and
          rained on. Zero fluff.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What&rsquo;s next:</strong> I&rsquo;m presenting at Mountain Readiness
          (Fallout 2026 and Lonestar 2027), the podcast is coming back for a brand-new season,
          and the Ghost&rsquo;s next big upgrade is on the horizon &mdash; an FSR Aspen Lite XL
          rooftop tent. Stick around. Bring marshmallows.
        </p>
        <p class="about-cta">
          <a href="/podcast" class="btn">Listen to the podcast</a>
          <a
            href="https://www.instagram.com/ghostsubieadventures"
            class="btn btn-outline"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >Follow @ghostsubieadventures</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-photos">
        <img
          class="framed about-main"
          src="/images/family-selfie.jpg"
          alt="Roman with his wife Michelle and their son Jonah, smiling around a campfire"
        />
        <img
          class="framed"
          src="/images/roman-basecamp.jpg"
          alt="Roman standing with the Ghost, his white Subaru Forester, at a Subaru Base Camp event"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-split { align-items: start; padding-bottom: 4.5rem; }
  .about-photos { display: grid; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .about-main {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    /* Jonah is front-left in this selfie — keep him in frame */
    object-position: 20% 80%;
  }
  .about-photos .framed { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  .about-cta { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
</style>
